v=item('ex-the-soergel-functor-on-a-small-regular-block','example','The Soergel functor on the small regular sl_2 block',common+['thm-indecomposable-projectives-correspond-to-indecomposable-soergel-modules','prop-verma-flag-multiplicities-are-standard-filtration-ranks-under-v','def-type-a-soergel-bimodule-for-a-simple-reflection','def-type-a-standard-graph-bimodules-support-filtrations-and-character'],r'''Assume the Axiom of Choice inherited from the category-O suppliers. Work over k=C in the dominant regular integral sl_2 block at lambda=0, with rho=1 and W={e,s}, so s dot 0=-2. Put Delta_e=M(0), Delta_s=M(-2)=L(-2), P_e=P(0)=Delta_e and P_s=P(-2). There are nonsplit sequences 0→L(-2)→Delta_e→L(0)→0 and 0→Delta_e→P_s→Delta_s→0. With C=k[x]/(x²), deg x=2, and V=Hom(P_s,-), the left C-module values are V(P_e)=k=C/(x), V(P_s)=C, V(Delta_e)=V(Delta_s)=k, V(L(0))=0 and V(L(-2))=k. The projective Hom table, with rows as sources P_e,P_s and columns as targets P_e,P_s, is ((k,k),(k,C)); thus the four dimensions are ((1,1),(1,2)). Choose i:k→C, i(1)=x, and p:C→k, p(a+bx)=a. Under the Struktursatz these are the nonzero mixed projective maps, with p i=0 and i p=m_x, multiplication by x. This explicitly computes End(P_s)=C and the projective full-faithfulness comparison, rather than claiming full faithfulness on the whole block. For S=k[a], s(a)=-a, the polynomial lifts B_e=S and B_s=S⊗_{k[a²]}S(1) reduce on the right to k and C(1); their labels are e^{-1}=e and s^{-1}=s. The centered auxiliary degrees on C(1) are -1,1. Before reduction the standard graph ranks (e,s) are (1,0) for B_e and (1,1) for B_s, agreeing with the Verma-flag multiplicities of P_e and P_s at v=1. These ranks are taken before graph supports coalesce at the origin; no grading on arbitrary O objects or intrinsic separated-support filtration on V(P) is asserted.''',r'''Use only the named current A-page suppliers and explicit rank-one algebra. In the PBW basis f^n v of M(t), e f^n v=n(t-n+1)f^{n-1}v. At t=0, f v is a singular vector generating M(-2), and the quotient is the one-dimensional L(0); at t=-2 every n>0 coefficient is nonzero, proving simplicity. Highest-weight generation gives nonsplitting of the first sequence. The empty-word case of the projective-generation lemma makes Delta_e=P_e; its one-wall case and the two-step extension lemma give the second sequence and P_s. Since Hom(P_s,L_y) is k for its head y=s and zero for y=e, exactness of V and the displayed composition factors give dimensions 1,2,1,1,0,1 in the stated order. Endomorphismensatz identifies V(P_s) with the regular C-module. The only one-dimensional C-module has x acting by zero, identifying every nonzero dimension-one value with k. Compute Hom_C(k,k)=k, Hom_C(k,C)=kx (annihilator of x), Hom_C(C,k)=k and Hom_C(C,C)=C. Struktursatz with projective targets identifies the four actual O-Hom spaces and compositions; normalize i,p so i(1)=x and p(1)=1, then pi=0 and ip=m_x on the basis 1,x. Independently, the polynomial model for B_s is k[l,r]/(l²-r²)(1). Right reduction r=0 gives k[l]/l²(1). The submodule (l-r) is free rank one on graph l=-r and the quotient is free rank one on graph l=r; the annihilator of l-r is (l+r), since cancellation in k[l,r] is valid. Thus its two standard graph layers have ranks one each. The e lift has only the e graph. Compare the two once-each/one-only Verma flags, invoking the existing multiplicity supplier with total ranks only. The fixed average coordinate in the published two-variable permutation realization is split off and killed on reduction, as explicitly allowed by the existing A-page dictionary. These finite computations illustrate those suppliers, rather than proving their general claims.''')
ce=item('cex-soergel-full-faithfulness-does-not-hold-on-all-category-o-objects','counterexample','The Soergel functor is not fully faithful on all category-O objects',common+['thm-simple-objects-of-category-o-are-highest-weight-modules'],r'''Assume the inherited Axiom of Choice. The assertion that V=Hom(P(-2),-) is fully faithful on every object of the regular integral sl_2 block at lambda=0 is false. Let L_0=L(0) be the nonzero one-dimensional simple. Then V(L_0)=0 and the nonzero identity in Hom_O(L_0,L_0)=k maps to zero in Hom_C(0,0)=0: V is not faithful. It also fails fullness on Hom_O(M(0),L(-2)): that Hom space is zero, whereas V(M(0))=V(L(-2))=k=C/(x) and Hom_C(k,k)=k. Both counterexamples have a nonprojective target, so they do not contradict the Struktursatz, which requires its target Q to be projective (and allows an arbitrary source). Passing to the quotient by the V-killed Serre subcategory is a separate assertion and is not refuted.''',r'''Compute directly, without relying on another generated B example as a supplier. In the PBW basis, e f^n v=n(t-n+1)f^{n-1}v shows the nonsplit 0→L(-2)→M(0)→L(0)→0 and simplicity of M(-2)=L(-2). P(-2) has unique simple head L(-2), so its Hom to L(0) is zero and its Hom to L(-2) is one dimensional. Exactness of Hom(P(-2),-) then gives V(M(0)) one dimensional; x²=0 makes x act zero on both one-dimensional values. A homomorphism M(0)→L(-2) must send its cyclic highest-weight vector of weight0 to a weight0 vector. The weights of L(-2) are -2,-4,..., so no such vector exists and the Hom is zero. Thus the induced zero→k map is not onto. End(L(0))=k follows directly from its one-dimensional underlying space, giving the independent failure of faithfulness. L(0) is nonprojective since the first nonsplit epimorphism onto it would otherwise split. L(-2) is nonprojective since the nonsplit 0→M(0)→P(-2)→L(-2)→0 from the existing two-step wall extension would otherwise split. State the target-projective hypothesis explicitly; do not replace it by the weaker both-projective wording.''')
w=item('ex-wall-crossing-on-projectives-in-the-sl-two-block','example','Wall-crossing on the projectives in the sl_2 block',common+['def-wall-crossing-functor-and-unit-counit','thm-wall-crossing-under-the-soergel-functor-is-tensoring-with-the-coinvariant-soergel-bimodule','prop-translation-functors-are-exact-and-biadjoint-across-a-wall'],r'''Assume the inherited Axiom of Choice. In the regular integral sl_2 block with lambda=0, rho=1, s dot 0=-2 and singular wall weight mu=-1, the indecomposable projectives are P_e=M(0) and P_s=P(-2). The wall-crossing functor theta_s satisfies theta_s(P_e)≅P_s and theta_s(P_s)≅P_s⊕P_s. In ordered projective bases (P_e,P_s), its matrix, with columns as inputs, is ((0,0),(1,2)). On the Soergel side C=k[x]/(x²), C^s=k and V(P_e)=k, V(P_s)=C; hence V theta_s(P_e)=C⊗_k k≅C and V theta_s(P_s)=C⊗_k C≅C⊕C as left C-modules. The latter tensor is the four-dimensional coinvariant bimodule (left C acts on the first factor), while the right-reduced polynomial B_s is only two dimensional. The result computes wall-crossing on projective objects, in addition to the preserved existing computation on Verma modules.''',r'''For the first equality, apply the existing projective-generation and two-step wall-extension lemmas to the one-letter reduced word: theta_s M(0)=P(-2), with standard flag M(0),M(-2). For the second equality, exact biadjoint translation preserves projectives. Apply theta_s to the flag 0→M(0)→P_s→M(-2)→0. Its two outer values are P_s by the existing rank-one two-step extension, so theta_s P_s has standard multiplicities (2,2). Every projective in this two-simple block is a sum of P_e and P_s, whose flags have multiplicities (1,0),(1,1) by BGG reciprocity. The equations a+b=2 and b=2 give a=0,b=2, proving the object isomorphism without treating a class identity as an isomorphism by itself. Alternatively compute with the existing wall-crossing-under-V theorem: s(x)=-x gives C^s=k; the left C-linear isomorphism C⊕C→C⊗_k C sends (u,v) to u⊗1+v⊗x. The projective Struktursatz reflects this isomorphism because all objects concerned are projective. Display both tensor basis and projective multiplicity calculation; no generated B item is a dependency.''')
